TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"The text calls the orbit geostationary at 600 km altitude. Geostationary orbit is near 35,786 km altitude above Earth’s equator, with a roughly 24-hour period; a 600 km orbit is low Earth orbit and cannot remain fixed above the reef."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"The mission’s asserted near-real-time relay and continuous fixed coverage are not supported by a feasible orbit, constellation, ground segment, or communications analysis."},{"where":"Image 1","issue":"The chart schedules finalisation in weeks 9–10, while the accompanying text says weeks 7 and 8 are reserved for review, amendments, final simulations, and reflection."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The claim that oceans have become 30 percent more acidic is imprecise; ocean surface acidity has increased by about 30 percent (a decrease in pH), not that acidity itself is generally measured as a simple percentage."}],"overall":"The report presents a relevant Australian mission concept and a usable timetable, but the preliminary design remains largely prospective. The proposed 600 km geostationary orbit is fundamentally incorrect, and there are no technical results. STK is mentioned and tutorials are reported, but software selection and planned information sources need clearer treatment.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The need, broad mission function, and likely users are identifiable, with supporting sources. However, the proposed satellite’s capabilities and requirements remain vague: there is no defined instrument, coverage, revisit, or resolution, and the discussion does not clearly establish how the satellite itself would provide near-real-time service.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"This tool could be applied to a new satellite over the Great Barrier Reef."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":15.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A timetable is provided with task descriptions and a sequence of work, including launch, orbit, communications, and STK activities. It is mission-relevant but has limited contingency planning, and planned information sources are not systematically identified. The chart indicates work continuing through week 10, while the text says finalisation is reserved for weeks 7 and 8.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"The goal is to brainstorm and research as many possible strategies for the satellite’s launch/orbit and then gradually cut and refine them over the next few weeks"},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Deficient","mark":3.0,"scale":10.0,"points":3.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"The submission reports background reading and software tutorials, but includes no preliminary technical results, calculations, design outputs, or interpretation. The stated orbit is technically incorrect, so it does not demonstrate sound progress on mission design.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner’s monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity, and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":12.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report uses headings, readable prose, a labelled Gantt chart, and source links. Presentation is generally understandable, but citations are bare URLs and footnote markers are not consistently integrated into a formal reference list. The chart and narrative also contain a schedule inconsistency, and the report lacks a distinct software-selection explanation.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"¹ https://www.noaa.gov/education/resource-collections/ocean-coasts/ocean-acidification"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""}]}]}
